# Generated files: collapsed by default in GitHub diffs and excluded from language stats.
#
# These are committed on purpose and MUST stay in the repository — EF Core needs the per-migration
# model snapshot to build the migration chain, and the OpenAPI client is the typed contract the
# front-ends compile against. What this file changes is only how they are PRESENTED: a reviewer sees
# them folded rather than scrolling past thousands of machine-written lines to reach the hand-written
# change.
#
# The motivating case: a single migration's `.Designer.cs` is ~2100 lines, which was 35% of PR #198
# regardless of how small the schema change was. Every future migration PR has the same shape.
#
# `linguist-generated` implies `-diff` (folded in the web UI) and `-linguist-detectable`. It does NOT
# make git ignore the file, and it does NOT stop `git diff` showing it locally — use
# `git diff -- ':!*.Designer.cs'` for that.

# EF Core migration snapshots — regenerated by `dotnet ef migrations add`, never hand-edited.
# NOTE: the migration BODY (`<timestamp>_<Name>.cs`) is deliberately NOT listed. It is routinely
# hand-edited in this repository — raw SQL for exclusion constraints, and the compatibility views
# feature 003 added — so it must stay fully visible in review.
*.Designer.cs linguist-generated=true
api/Platform/Data/Migrations/LeapDbContextModelSnapshot.cs linguist-generated=true

# OpenAPI client — regenerated by `npm run generate --workspace @leap/api-client`.
packages/api-client/generated/** linguist-generated=true

# Shell scripts and the generated OpenAPI snapshot MUST be LF: CRLF breaks bash on Linux CI, and a
# CRLF snapshot would fail the #141 freshness check, which regenerates with LF on the Linux runner.
*.sh text eol=lf
api/Modules/Compass/Contracts/compass-v1.openapi.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
